    {
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "What model? I am not aware of a 70B model, please don't leave useless comments like this without context. This project won't magicly make your models use less memory, you need new models trained from scratch that are bigger. As is it seems no one has really done this, for what reason, likely goes over my head. Could be technical or just no one wanting to take the risk, not sure what's blocking it really. Not even Microsoft seems willing at the moment, maybe we could see a surprise announcement with their Phi models but doubt it, I do hope they do though and I do encourage them to maybe. Like I said previously I think 120B would be sweet spot for me if it scales in terms of memory like I imagine.\n\nAs for risks, stop fearing your computer. This is likely the single best advice you will get, unless your computer is overheating, your overclocking it, etc. Computers usually don't tend to randomly explode in my experience. So have fun and experiment a little, worst that happens in you lose your work and quite possibly your time. :-)\n\nIf you mean AI safety, I am not qualified or really care to be I'll leave it there. However, this likely has no effect on that regardless common sense tells me, other than possibly giving more powerful models locally to us plebs without a few h100s in their bedroom.\n\nP.s. I don't mean to come off as mean spirited, if I did my bad",
